From dfd5d4fd3243cccf8d22645ca8769b4dc023e139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: decklink-linux-anon
 <358323356+decklink-linux-anon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:41:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] ui: External Video Output on a DeckLink card (Linux)

Settings > Playback > Enable External Video Output (playback.enableTransmit)
now sends the Program monitor's sequence frame to the host's VideoOutput;
the desktop app's is DeckLink device 0 at 1080p25 (apps/filmcraft
video_out.rs). Elsewhere the setting stays greyed out as before.

- ui-egui stays OS-independent: HostHooks::open_video_output and the
  VideoOutput trait; transmit.rs owns the open output.
- Frames are requested at the size that fits 1920x1080, through the frame
  server like the monitors. Paused: the playhead frame is sent once.
  Playing: the next frames are scheduled and each is sent once when ready.
- GPU path (default): the workers plan and prepare frames for the
  off-screen device; a transmit-gpu thread composites and reads them back
  and hands them to the card. CPU compositor frames are the fallback.
- A missing card or driver is logged once; the output is retried when the
  setting is toggled. Turning it off releases the card.
- While playing, a log line every 5 s gives frames sent / skipped and the
  stage timings.

Tests: transmit unit tests and tests/it/transmit_ui.rs (setting off, paused
frame once at output size, playback, CPU fallback, GPU path, no card,
release on toggle; an ignored throughput benchmark).
